---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ContentTable from '../../components/ContentTable.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LANG_TAGS } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { facts } from '../../lib/facts';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const F = facts(lang);
/** Date this page last changed (no cookies, Clarity in cookieless mode). */
const PAGE_UPDATED = '2026-10-06';
const updated = displayDate(PAGE_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS[lang]);
const title = `Cookie policy Poland ${F.year}: naretke.pl sets no cookies`;
const description = `Cookies on naretke.pl in ${F.year}: the site sets no cookies and keeps none of your salary inputs. Page stability is checked anonymously with Microsoft Clarity.`;
const summary = [
  ['Site cookies', 'None'],
  ['Analytics or advertising cookies', 'None'],
  ['Browser storage (localStorage, sessionStorage)', 'Not used by the calculator'],
  ['Stability check (Microsoft Clarity)', 'Anonymous, cookieless'],
];
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: label('home', lang), path: route('home', lang) }, { name: label('cookies', lang), path: route('cookies', lang) }])]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: label('cookies', lang) }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies and similar technologies</h1>
    <p class="lead">The short answer: naretke.pl stores no cookies on your device. How data is handled is explained in the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>At a glance</h2>
    <ContentTable headers={['Type', 'On naretke.pl']} rows={summary} />

    <h2>Your figures stay in the browser tab</h2>
    <p>Net pay, ZUS contributions, the health contribution and PIT advance are worked out by a script in your browser. Gross pay, contract type (employment, mandate, specific-work or B2B), the PIT-2 form, youth relief or PPK are not written to a cookie, to <code>localStorage</code> or to any other browser storage, and they are gone once you close the tab. To keep a calculation, copy the result link: the figures then live in the page address, not in a cookie. Since nothing is stored, there is no cookie banner either: there is nothing to accept.</p>

    <h2>Anonymous stability check</h2>
    <p>To spot when the calculator stops working, a page loads too slowly or a button does nothing, the site runs Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode. Clarity then creates none of <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>, gives every page view its own single-use identifier and does not join your visits together. Page text and form fields are masked in the browser before anything leaves it.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The site shows no ads and loads no advertising or social media pixels.</p>

    <h2>Blocking this check too</h2>
    <p>If you would rather not have even this anonymous check, block the <code>clarity.ms</code> domain in your browser or with a content blocker. The salary calculator works exactly the same.</p>

    <h2>The widget on other sites</h2>
    <p>The calculator embedded in a frame on other websites does not load Clarity and stores nothing on the device.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Version dated {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
